<title>USA: Labor talks start at Reynolds can plant.</title>
<headline>Labor talks start at Reynolds can plant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor talks have begun at Reynolds Metals Co's Salisbury aluminum beverage can plant in North Carolina, said Cheryl Jones, a company spokeswoman.</p>
<p>&quot;The labor negotiations are underway, but our policy is not to comment on the process itself,&quot; Jones said.</p>
<p>Labor union Aluminum, Brick and Glass Workers International and Reynolds Metals are seeking a new deal to replace a three-year pact which expires Nov 30.</p>
<p>ABGW officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>--New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
</text>
